       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum prescription dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. That much ibuprofen carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common maximum anti-inflammatory regimen\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the absolute ceiling, usually for short courses\n\nIf 1,600 mg four times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
